sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User (Telegram)
    participant P as TaskIntentParser
    participant I as IdempotencyManager
    participant E as Domain Engine<br/>(Task/Project/Workflow/...)
    participant B as EventBus
    participant PR as ProjectionEngine
    participant RM as Read Models<br/>(Tasks / LIFE_*)
    participant TL as LIFE_TIMELINE
    participant EX as Life Execution OS<br/>(future, reads only)

    U->>P: "帮我建一个续签保险的任务，下周三前完成"
    P->>I: parsed intent + params
    I->>E: createTask / createProject / ...
    E->>B: publish(TASK_CREATED / PROJECT_CREATED / ...)
    B->>PR: dispatch(event)
    PR->>RM: upsert row (single source of truth: Events)
    PR->>TL: append timeline entry (always, regardless of entity type)
    Note over EX: Execution subscribes to Events independently.<br/>Domain never calls Execution directly.
    EX-->>B: (reads) TASK_CREATED, TASK_COMPLETED, ...
    EX->>EX: place Reference in EXEC_VIEWS.Today (no data copy)

    U->>E: completeTask(task_id)
    E->>B: publish(TASK_COMPLETED)
    B->>PR: dispatch(event)
    PR->>RM: Tasks.status=DONE, remove from ActiveTasks
    PR->>TL: append timeline entry
    EX-->>B: (reads) TASK_COMPLETED
    EX->>EX: update its own Today View display

    Note over E,B: Conversion example — Task to Project
    U->>E: convertTaskToProject(task_id, projectMeta)
    E->>B: publish(TASK_CONVERTED_TO_PROJECT)
    B->>PR: dispatch(event)
    PR->>RM: Tasks.status=CONVERTED (source Task)
    PR->>RM: LIFE_PROJECTS insert (new Project, source_task_id set)
    PR->>TL: append 2 entries (closes Task lineage, opens Project lineage)

    Note over E,B: v5.1 — reverse direction, Project to Task
    U->>E: convertProjectToTask(project_id, taskMeta)
    Note over E: precondition: no sub-projects,<br/>no non-terminal child Tasks
    E->>B: publish(PROJECT_CONVERTED_TO_TASK)
    B->>PR: dispatch(event)
    PR->>RM: LIFE_PROJECTS.status=CONVERTED_TO_TASK (source Project)
    PR->>RM: Tasks insert (new Task, source_project_id set)
    PR->>TL: append 2 entries (mirror image of the Task-to-Project case)
